WEBVTT

00:17:30.036 --> 00:17:31.236
So this is what we do.

00:17:31.236 --> 00:17:34.476
This is how, again, looking backward
can move you forward.

00:17:34.476 --> 00:17:36.916
Lily, that's such a fantastic --

00:17:37.596 --> 00:17:40.556
People in the chat are saying,
"We will hold Lily accountable,"

00:17:40.556 --> 00:17:41.756
which I love.

00:17:41.756 --> 00:17:43.956
So Lily, thanks for that.

00:17:43.996 --> 00:17:45.516
We're going to bring --

00:17:45.556 --> 00:17:48.076
I really, really appreciate
your sharing that with us,

00:17:48.076 --> 00:17:51.196
and I want you to report back
that you did speak up.

00:17:51.236 --> 00:17:52.596
L: I will, thank you.

00:17:52.636 --> 00:17:53.956
DHP: Thanks, Lily.

00:17:54.276 --> 00:17:57.036
WPR: Well, we have a question here
from Claudia, who asks,

00:17:57.076 --> 00:17:59.916
"Can you speak to the issue
of painful life regrets?

00:17:59.956 --> 00:18:01.436
Major opportunities lost?